  "worked_solution": "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{z}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}({x}^{2}{z}^{3}\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{zy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{z}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({f}_{z}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{zyx}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{zy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zyx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({f}_{zy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{y}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3x{z}^{2}}{\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{zyx}(x,y,z)$ at $(2,4,-2):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zyx}(2,4,-2) & =\\frac{3(2)(-2)^{2}}{\\sqrt{4}}=\\frac{24}{2}=12\\end{aligned}\n$$",
